# HTTP response headers for Codeberg Pages (git-pages, Netlify `_headers` format).
#
# git-pages denies custom headers by default:
#
#   AllowedCustomHeaders []string `toml:"allowed-custom-headers"
#                                  default:"[\"X-Clacks-Overhead\"]"`
#   — https://codeberg.org/git-pages/git-pages/src/branch/main/src/config.go
#
# A rule containing even ONE non-allowlisted header is discarded *whole*
# (`validateHeaderRule` -> `AddProblem` -> `continue`, src/headers.go), and only
# the first matching rule is applied per URL (`matchPathRules`) — extra `/*`
# blocks do not stack. That is why the old single `/*` rule listing HSTS,
# Referrer-Policy, COOP/COEP/CORP and X-Frame-Options served *nothing*, not
# even X-Clacks-Overhead.
#
# ── ALLOWLIST PROBE (temporary — delete once answered) ──────────────────────
# The earlier test proved "at least one of those headers is refused", not
# "all of them are". Each candidate below sits on its own path so a refusal
# can only take down its own rule. After this deploys, run:
#
#   curl -sI https://larmart.de/robots.txt  | grep -i x-frame-options
#   curl -sI https://larmart.de/humans.txt  | grep -i cross-origin-resource
#   curl -sI https://larmart.de/favicon.svg | grep -i strict-transport
#   curl -sI https://larmart.de/sw.js       | grep -i content-security-policy
#
# Whatever comes back is allowlisted and can move into the `/*` rule below.
# Anything that stays silent is refused by git-pages and is not achievable
# on this host. These paths lose X-Clacks-Overhead while the probe is in
# place, because only the first matching rule applies.

/robots.txt
  X-Frame-Options: DENY

/humans.txt
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin

/favicon.svg
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains

/sw.js
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'

# ── Live rule ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff is already sent by git-pages itself.
# Referrer-Policy is delivered via <meta name="referrer"> in BaseLayout.astro.
# The real CSP ships as an Astro-generated <meta> with per-build hashes.

/*
  X-Clacks-Overhead: GNU Terry Pratchett
